      {
        "id": 208204,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-08T05:32:08.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm slightly annoyed we don't know Spite's RPG future. I get spoilers, but I was really interested in the power dynamic between him and Gloomy and the Master. Actually, if we didn't know The Master was on Gloomy's throne, I'd bet money that's where we would find Jack.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I was also nearly certain for a moment that Demon's Kiss and Mind Phyre were going to be revealed as components of Zhu Long's concotion, but I'd still place some small amount of money of there being a connection there, maybe an offshoot inspired by the original.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thing is, it is odd to get life-draining powers and psychic powers and purple fire powers from normal drugs. I almost wish they had just called Spite a mystical force and been done with it because comic's science makes less sense to me than magical forces, especially when they exist side by side.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, am I the only one considering making an RPG character based off Spite now? Some poor sap who got kidnapped by Pike Scientists and the heroes saved just a little too late, getting a dosage of Spite's highly Toxic blood which they purchased from FILTER, and having to deal with this need to drain the life energy from people, but the morality that prevents the kinds of murder sprees that Spite went on. Can the blood of a monster be turned towards noble ends?</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
