      {
        "id": 208208,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-08T17:12:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"mwc146\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n mwc146:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My impression of what they said about his RPG future was along the lines of, \"We don't have anything planned, but it's totally possible that the clones are under there somewhere, so you could probably do something with it.\"Basically, every summation of what they have planned with the RPG ends with an unspoken, \"But if you want to do otherwise, that's cool too.\"</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>But remember how they ended the episode, calling back to spite as \"The monster that can't be killed\" I feel like there is some heavy implications that the original Spite is going to be making an appearance somehow, because he's totally dead now that Gloomweaver took over that body and power and kicked him out right? Just like when Parse totally killed him? Or that building fell on him?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The clones aren't a surprise because of Iron Legacy and Broken City, so if they were going to use them I feel like they would just say so, but if Spite's Animus somehow found another body, that would be somewhat shocking, and hopefully be a \"fix\" for the dissatisfaction felt with Gloom Spite.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
