      {
        "id": 208212,
        "name": "Chaosmancer",
        "username": "Chaosmancer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-09T00:24:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jeysie\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/48/1868_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jeysie:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Spite's flavor as a remorseless spree killer just out for funsies has its appeal, but it's also increasingly one-note as the storyline goes on.In contrast, other awful villains tend to either have style (Apostate, Heartbreaker), or some sort of grand scheme beyond merely mayhem (Biomancer, Voss), making them easier to keep doing more stuff with.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>True, but one thing about Spite is that (terrifyingly enough) he has room to grow.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>He is a genius-level intellect, he just doesn't use for it anything, so what if the Fleshwalker event was a last straw kind of deal. Spite ends up out of his body, floating around in impotent rage, and realizess that if he wants to destroy the Wraith and the other heroes, and possibly get bacl at Gloomweaver, he needs to start planning more. He's got to set more short-term plans beyond \"eat enough to live\" and start gathering different types of power. He's smart enough to press down his instincts I think, which would be to smash everything.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Or, perhaps he does continue to just smash everything, but instead of eating people he spends some time eating spirits in the Realm of Discord, becoming a true monstrosity and force of the Universe.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>And sure, it's probably still one note, but if every couple of Halloweens we get a new \"Spite is terrifying and kills a bunch of people\" story, it can still be a fun read (and I just realized I was thinking about that in terms of Sentinel Comics readership… well done.)</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:38:04.184Z",
